<title>USA: Flow control impasse affects billions in muni debt.</title>
<headline>Flow control impasse affects billions in muni debt.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Seven state and local government groups showered Capitol Hill with letters on Wednesday warning that the U.S. Congress' failure to pass a bill to protect up to $20 billion in solid-waste facilities debt is having a mounting impact on bond issuers nationwide.</p>
<p>The groups said in a two-page letter that a total of $3.37 billion in solid waste debt has been downgraded by the nation's three top municipal bond rating agencies or listed as unstable or on &quot;credit watch.&quot; They detailed the impact of Congress' inaction on 37 towns and counties nationwide.</p>
</text>
